# PLACEHOLDER. The owner replaces this whole file with the real public key.
#
# This is not a key. The Linux release workflow refuses to sign while this file has no armoured
# public key block, and fails when REQUIRE_LINUX_SIGNING is "true".
#
# To publish the key (see docs/releasing.md, "Signing the Linux files"):
#   1. Export it:   gpg --armor --export <fingerprint> > docs/scrim-release-key.asc
#   2. Put the full 40 character fingerprint in linuxSigningFingerprint in
#      apps/landing/src/site.config.ts.
#   3. Store the private key and its passphrase as the repository secrets LINUX_SIGNING_KEY
#      (armoured, from: gpg --armor --export-secret-keys <fingerprint>) and LINUX_SIGNING_PASSPHRASE.
#
# Never commit the private key.
